              <span class="project-badge">[ Python ]</span>
              <span class="project-badge">[ FastAPI ]</span>
              <span class="project-badge">[ YOLOv8 ]</span>
              <span class="project-badge">[ NumPy ]</span>
              <span class="project-badge">[ Gemini AI ]</span>
              <span class="project-badge">[ OpenCV ]</span>
            </div>
            <div class="project-card-expanded">
              <div class="project-card-details">
                <div class="project-detail-block">
                  <span class="project-detail-label">Overview</span>
                  <p>Built and deployed a full-stack medical-imaging application (React client, FastAPI backend) that runs YOLOv8 inference to detect and segment coronary stenosis in angiograms, with a geometry-based severity classifier.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="project-detail-block">
                  <span class="project-detail-label">Key Features</span>
                  <ul>
                    <li>Benchmarked 3 YOLOv8 variants (n, s, m) for detection and instance segmentation on coronary angiography images</li>
                    <li>5-endpoint FastAPI API serving detection, segmentation, and heatmap overlays with structured JSON responses</li>
                    <li>Geometry-based classifier calculating percentage stenosis from reference and minimum lumen diameters, mapped to 5 severity levels</li>
                    <li>React frontend with interactive visualization of detection results and stenosis measurements</li>
                    <li>Automated preprocessing pipeline with OpenCV for image normalization and augmentation</li>
                  </ul>
                </div>
                <div class="project-detail-block">
                  <span class="project-detail-label">Architecture</span>
                  <p>React.js frontend consuming a FastAPI backend that hosts multiple YOLOv8 model variants. NumPy-powered geometric analysis computes stenosis percentage from lumen diameters. Model outputs include bounding boxes, segmentation masks, and Grad-CAM heatmaps for clinical interpretability.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="project-detail-block">
                  <span class="project-detail-label">Impact</span>
                  <p class="project-card-metric">3 YOLOv8 variants benchmarked · 5 REST endpoints · 5-level severity classification · Sub-200ms inference · React + FastAPI full-stack deployment</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="project-card-actions">
